{
  "info": {
    "name": "Translator - LibreTranslate API tests",
    "description": "Tests the LibreTranslate load balancer used by the Translator app (default http://127.0.0.1:5000). The server runs separately: start it with LibreTranslateServer\\start.cmd (settings in LibreTranslateServer\\config.json).\n\nLoad balancer test routes:\n- GET  /lb/health    quick check: 200 / 503\n- GET  /lb/status    every backend with counters\n- GET  /lb/selftest  real test of every worker: 200 when all pass, 503 + details when any fails\n\nLibreTranslate routes (forwarded to a worker):\n- GET  /languages\n- POST /detect      {\"q\": \"text\"}\n- POST /translate   {\"q\": \"text\" or [..], \"source\": \"auto\"|code, \"target\": code, \"format\": \"text\"}\n\nNote: /translate with source \"auto\" and several texts detects ONE language for the whole batch. The app therefore calls /detect per text and translates with an explicit source (folder 3 shows this).\n\nFolders:\n1. Server and load balancer (test routes)\n2. Language detection\n3. Translation\n4. Data-driven: run with the Collection Runner and translation-data.csv\n5. Errors\n\nCommand-line alternative without Postman: LibreTranslateServer\\.venv\\Scripts\\python check_server.py",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:5000"
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Shared: log every response in the Postman Console",
          "try { console.log(pm.request.url.getPath(), pm.response.code, JSON.stringify(pm.response.json())); } catch (e) { }"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Server and load balancer",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health (quick)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 (at least one backend healthy)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const h = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Status is ok (all backends healthy)', () => pm.expect(h.status).to.eql('ok'));",
                  "pm.test('healthy equals total', () => pm.expect(h.healthy).to.eql(h.total));",
                  "pm.test('Answers in under 1 second', () => pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(1000));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "description": "Quick liveness check answered by the load balancer itself. 200 when at least one backend is healthy, 503 when none is. status: ok (all healthy), degraded (some), down (none).",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/lb/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "lb",
                "health"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Languages",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const codes = pm.response.json().map(l => l.code);",
                  "pm.test('English is loaded', () => pm.expect(codes).to.include('en'));",
                  "pm.test('French and Spanish are loaded', () => { pm.expect(codes).to.include('fr'); pm.expect(codes).to.include('es'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/languages",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "languages"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Load balancer status",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const s = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('At least one healthy backend', () => pm.expect(s.healthy).to.be.at.least(1));",
                  "pm.test('All backends healthy', () => pm.expect(s.healthy).to.eql(s.total));",
                  "console.log(s.backends.map(b => `${b.url} healthy=${b.healthy} active=${b.active} served=${b.served}`).join('\\n'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/lb/status",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "lb",
                "status"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Self-test every worker",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const r = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Status 200 (all backends passed)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Report says passed', () => pm.expect(r.passed).to.be.true);",
                  "pm.test('Every backend tested', () => pm.expect(r.backends.length).to.eql(r.backends_total));",
                  "r.backends.forEach(b => {",
                  "  pm.test(`${b.url}: all checks passed`, () => {",
                  "    const failed = b.checks.filter(c => !c.passed).map(c => `${c.check}: ${c.details}`);",
                  "    pm.expect(failed, failed.join('; ')).to.be.empty;",
                  "  });",
                  "  pm.test(`${b.url}: detection and translation were tested`, () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(b.checks.some(c => c.check.startsWith('detect'))).to.be.true;",
                  "    pm.expect(b.checks.some(c => c.check.startsWith('translate'))).to.be.true;",
                  "  });",
                  "});",
                  "console.log(r.backends.map(b => `${b.url} passed=${b.passed}: ` + b.checks.map(c => `${c.check}=${c.passed} (${c.ms} ms)`).join(', ')).join('\\n'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "description": "Real test of EVERY backend, sent to each one directly (not through the balancing): GET /languages, POST /detect of one sample per loaded language (must detect that language), and one POST /translate. 200 when all backends pass, 503 when any fails; the body lists every check with its result and time. Add ?api_key=KEY when the workers run with api_keys.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/lb/selftest",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "lb",
                "selftest"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Test routes of the load balancer (handled by it, not forwarded): /lb/health, /lb/status, /lb/selftest. Run this folder first: if it passes, every worker is working."
    },
